From: Matěj Cepl <mcepl@cepl.eu>
Subject: auth: shut down the OAuth callback server gracefully

The loopback callback handler hands the authorization code to
OAuthLogin before its response is flushed. OAuthLogin may then
exchange the code and return, and the deferred server.Close()
closes active connections at once, so the browser (or the test
client) gets EOF instead of "Authorization received".

Use server.Shutdown() with a short timeout, which waits for
in-flight responses to finish, and fall back to Close().

This made TestOAuthLoginOpensAuthorizationURLInBrowser fail
intermittently in OBS with:
  Get "http://127.0.0.1:NNNN?code=valid-code&state=...": EOF
Index: b/internal/auth/oauth.go
===================================================================
--- a/internal/auth/oauth.go
+++ b/internal/auth/oauth.go
@@ -109,7 +109,14 @@
 			}
 		}
 	}()
-	defer server.Close()
+	// Shut down gracefully so the browser receives the callback response before the connection closes.
+	defer func() {
+		shutdownCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.WithoutCancel(parent), time.Second)
+		defer cancel()
+		if server.Shutdown(shutdownCtx) != nil {
+			_ = server.Close()
+		}
+	}()
 	authorizeURL := config.AuthCodeURL(state, oauth2.S256ChallengeOption(verifier))
 	if opts.Authorize == nil {
 		return Credential{}, errors.New("OAuth requires an authorization URL handler")
